  "details": "Currently, implementing a branching (useful) dialog system in a world is tremendously inefficient. In practice, it ends up requiring either hundreds of gameobjects for all the dialog states which each just have an instance of a “data structure” script on them, or an editor script that converts something like a json “dialog map” document into a single script with possibly hundreds of thousands of lines of U# on one game object. Both of these are non-starters for most. It makes sense for this to just be a Unity component where a dev can feed a list of dialog states into it, and call methods on it from UI buttons or Udon. This would be dramatically more performant and use less space.",
